## 5.  Security Essentials

| Layer | What to Secure | Java Tooling |
|-------|----------------|--------------|
| **Transport** | TLS/SSL | `HttpsURLConnection`, `java.net.http.HttpClient`, Spring Security |
| **Authentication** | API keys, OAuth2 | Spring Security OAuth2, Keycloak adapters |
| **Authorization** | Role/Scope checks | Spring Security @PreAuthorize, JWT |
| **Input validation** | Avoid injection attacks | OWASP Java Encoder, built‑in validation (Jakarta Bean Validation) |
| **Rate limiting & throttling** | DDoS protection | Bucket4j, Resilience4j |
| **Secrets management** | Store passwords, keys | HashiCorp Vault, Kubernetes Secrets, Spring Cloud Vault |

> **Tip:** In Spring Boot, add `spring-boot-starter-security` and configure `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter` (or the newer lambda DSL). Use `OAuth2ResourceServer` for bearer‑token validation.

