Below is a **minimal, working** network‑based Tic‑Tac‑Toe game written in Java 17 (or any newer JDK) that uses **JavaFX** for the UI and plain **TCP sockets** for communication.  
The whole project consists of only two Java files:

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `TicTacToeServer.java` | Runs a simple server that accepts two clients, alternates turns, validates moves and pushes the updated board to both players. |
| `TicTacToeClient.java` | JavaFX GUI that connects to the server, lets you click cells, shows the opponent’s moves and the game result. |

> **Why this is “the simplest”**  
> * No external libraries – only JDK & JavaFX.  
> * Only one thread on the client (UI + a listening thread).  
> * Server logic is a single loop – no fancy concurrency or protocols.  
> * The communication protocol is human‑readable (`MOVE r c`, `UPDATE …`, `YOUR_TURN`, `END …`).  
> * Works out‑of‑the‑box on Windows, macOS, or Linux.

---

## 1. Prerequisites

| Item | Version | How to get it |
|------|---------|---------------|
| JDK | 17+ (or 8‑JDK with JavaFX bundled) | <https://jdk.java.net/> |
| JavaFX SDK | 17+ (same version as JDK) | <https://openjfx.io/> |

> **Note**: Starting with JDK 11 JavaFX is no longer bundled.  
> Download the SDK that matches your JDK, unzip it and remember the path to the `lib` folder.

---

## 2. The Server

```java
/*  TicTacToeServer.java  */
import java.io.*;
import java.net.*;
import java.util.Arrays;

public class TicTacToeServer {
    private static final int PORT = 5555;
    private static final String EMPTY = ".";
    private static final int SIZE = 3;

    private char[][] board = new char[SIZE][SIZE];
    private PrintWriter outX, outO;
    private BufferedReader inX, inO;
    private char turn = 'X'; // X always starts

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        new TicTacToeServer().start();
    }

    private void start() throws IOException {
        // initialise empty board
        for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++) Arrays.fill(board[i], EMPTY.charAt(0));

        try (ServerSocket ss = new ServerSocket(PORT)) {
            System.out.println("Tic‑Tac‑Toe Server started on port " + PORT);
            System.out.println("Waiting for Player X to connect…");
            Socket socketX = ss.accept();
            System.out.println("Player X connected.");

            System.out.println("Waiting for Player O to connect…");
            Socket socketO = ss.accept();
            System.out.println("Player O connected.");

            // set up readers/writers
            inX = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(socketX.getInputStream()));
            outX = new PrintWriter(socketX.getOutputStream(), true);
            inO = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(socketO.getInputStream()));
            outO = new PrintWriter(socketO.getOutputStream(), true);

            // tell players which symbol they are
            outX.println("SYMBOL X");
            outO.println("SYMBOL O");

            // Main game loop
            boolean gameRunning = true;
            while (gameRunning) {
                // Tell the player whose turn it is
                if (turn == 'X') {
                    outX.println("YOUR_TURN");
                    outO.println("WAIT");
                } else {
                    outO.println("YOUR_TURN");
                    outX.println("WAIT");
                }

                // Read the move from the current player
                BufferedReader currentIn = (turn == 'X' ? inX : inO);
                PrintWriter currentOut = (turn == 'X' ? outX : outO);

                String line = currentIn.readLine();
                if (line == null) {
                    // Client disconnected
                    gameRunning = false;
                    break;
                }

                // Expected format: MOVE r c   (0‑based indices)
                String[] parts = line.trim().split("\\s+");
                if (parts.length != 3 || !parts[0].equalsIgnoreCase("MOVE")) {
                    currentOut.println("ERROR Invalid command");
                    continue;
                }

                int r, c;
                try {
                    r = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);
                    c = Integer.parseInt(parts[2]);
                } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                    currentOut.println("ERROR Invalid coordinates");
                    continue;
                }

                if (!isValid(r, c)) {
                    currentOut.println("ERROR Cell occupied or out of bounds");
                    continue;
                }

                // Make the move
                board[r][c] = turn;
                // Broadcast board to both players
                broadcastBoard();

                // Check for win / draw
                if (hasWon(turn)) {
                    outX.println("END " + turn);
                    outO.println("END " + turn);
                    System.out.println("Player " + turn + " won.");
                    gameRunning = false;
                } else if (isDraw()) {
                    outX.println("END DRAW");
                    outO.println("END DRAW");
                    System.out.println("Game ended in a draw.");
                    gameRunning = false;
                } else {
                    // Switch turns
                    turn = (turn == 'X') ? 'O' : 'X';
                }
            }

            // Clean up
            socketX.close();
            socketO.close();
            System.out.println("Server shutting down.");
        }
    }

    private boolean isValid(int r, int c) {
        return r >= 0 && r < SIZE && c >= 0 && c < SIZE && board[r][c] == EMPTY.charAt(0);
    }

    private void broadcastBoard() {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        sb.append("UPDATE ");
        for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < SIZE; j++) {
                sb.append(board[i][j]);
            }
        }
        String boardMsg = sb.toString();
        outX.println(boardMsg);
        outO.println(boardMsg);
    }

    private boolean hasWon(char p) {
        // rows & columns
        for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++) {
            if (board[i][0] == p && board[i][1] == p && board[i][2] == p) return true;
            if (board[0][i] == p && board[1][i] == p && board[2][i] == p) return true;
        }
        // diagonals
        if (board[0][0] == p && board[1][1] == p && board[2][2] == p) return true;
        if (board[0][2] == p && board[1][1] == p && board[2][0] == p) return true;
        return false;
    }

    private boolean isDraw() {
        for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < SIZE; j++)
                if (board[i][j] == EMPTY.charAt(0))
                    return false;
        return true;
    }
}
```

**How the server works**

1. Listens on **port 5555**.  
2. Waits until two clients connect – the first client is **X**, the second is **O**.  
3. Main loop alternates turns, validates moves, updates the board, and notifies both clients.  
4. When a win or draw occurs the server sends `END <symbol>` or `END DRAW` and exits.

