while (round <= NUM_ROUNDS) {
    …
    else {              // this else is inside the loop
        int dealerBet = Math.min(...);   // <‑‑ duplicate declaration
        …
    }
}
```

Java does **not** allow a local variable to be redeclared in an inner block when the same‑named variable is still in scope in the outer block. The compiler therefore emits the “duplicate local variable” error.

---

### Fix

* Remove the inner declaration keyword **`int`** and just **assign** the value to the outer variable, or simply delete the outer variable and keep the inner one (but the outer one is needed later in the same method).  
