## 1. The Servlet

```java
package com.example.temperature;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import javax.servlet.ServletException;
import javax.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;      // optional – if you use annotations
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServlet;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;

/**
 * A very small servlet that converts Celsius to Fahrenheit.
 *
 * <p>
 *  * GET or POST parameter   :  celsius (e.g. 25 or 25.3)
 *  * Response (text/plain)  :  "25°C = 77°F"
 * </p>
 *
 * <p>
 *  The servlet can be deployed either by putting a <servlet> entry in web.xml
 *  or by using the @WebServlet annotation shown above.
 * </p>
 */
@WebServlet(name = "TemperatureConverterServlet", urlPatterns = {"/convert"})
public class TemperatureConverterServlet extends HttpServlet {

    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /*  Helper – the actual conversion.  The result is rounded to 2 digits */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    private double celsiusToFahrenheit(double celsius) {
        return celsius * 9.0 / 5.0 + 32.0;
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /*  GET – show a tiny form and handle the conversion in one step.    */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    @Override
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp)
            throws ServletException, IOException {

        String celsiusParam = req.getParameter("celsius");
        if (celsiusParam == null) {   // no input yet – just show the form
            showForm(resp, null, null);
            return;
        }

        double celsius;
        try {
            celsius = Double.parseDouble(celsiusParam);
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            // user typed something that isn’t a number
            showForm(resp, null, "Please enter a valid number");
            return;
        }

        double fahrenheit = celsiusToFahrenheit(celsius);
        showForm(resp, celsius, fahrenheit);
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /*  POST – same as GET – we forward the request to doGet().          */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    @Override
    protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp)
            throws ServletException, IOException {
        // Forward to doGet() so we don't duplicate code
        doGet(req, resp);
    }

    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    /*  Utility – render the simple HTML page.                            */
    /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
    private void showForm(HttpServletResponse resp,
                          Double celsius,
                          Double fahrenheit)
            throws IOException {

        resp.setContentType("text/html;charset=UTF-8");
        PrintWriter out = resp.getWriter();

        out.println("<!DOCTYPE html>");
        out.println("<html><head>");
        out.println("<title>Temperature Converter</title>");
        out.println("<style>");
        out.println("body {font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:2rem;}");
        out.println("label {display:inline-block;width:80px;}");
        out.println(".result {margin-top:1rem;font-weight:bold;}");
        out.println("</style>");
        out.println("</head><body>");

        out.println("<h1>Celsius → Fahrenheit</h1>");
        out.println("<form method='post'>");
        out.println("<label for='celsius'>Celsius:</label>");
        out.println("<input type='text' id='celsius' name='celsius' "
                    + (celsius != null ? "value='" + celsius + "'" : "") + ">");
        out.println("<input type='submit' value='Convert'>");
        out.println("</form>");

        if (celsius != null && fahrenheit != null) {
            out.println("<div class='result'>"
                    + String.format("%.2f°C = %.2f°F", celsius, fahrenheit)
                    + "</div>");
        }

        out.println("</body></html>");
    }
}
```

### What it does

| Step | What the code does |
|------|--------------------|
| 1 | `@WebServlet` registers the servlet under the URL pattern `/convert`. |
| 2 | `doGet()` is called on a **GET** or **POST** request (the latter simply forwards to `doGet()`). |
| 3 | It looks for the request parameter **celsius**. |
| 4 | If the parameter is missing, it just shows the form. |
| 5 | If the parameter is present, it parses it as a `double` and calls `celsiusToFahrenheit()`. |
| 6 | The form is redisplayed, now with the result (`celsius` and `fahrenheit` formatted to 2 decimal places). |
| 7 | If the input cannot be parsed, it displays an error message. |

