## 7. Advanced Features (Optional)

| Feature | How to enable |
|---------|---------------|
| **Hot‑reload** | Already implemented with the folder watcher. Keep the `js` folder in `<minecraft>/mods/kotlinjsmod/js`. |
| **Multiple modules** | Each `.js` file can `require` others. The loader caches them to avoid re‑evaluation. |
| **Interfacing with Minecraft** | In your Kotlin code, expose Java objects to Nashorn: `engine.put("minecraft", Minecraft.getMinecraft())`. JS can then call `minecraft.world.getBlockState(...)`. |
| **Security sandbox** | Use the Nashorn `--no-java` flag or set a `ClassFilter` to prevent modules from accessing arbitrary Java classes. |
| **Full Node integration** | If you want a true Node terminal, modify `spawnNodeProcess()` to point to a real Node project and use `nodeConsole` for logs. |
| **Performance tuning** | Keep the module cache; use `engine.eval(new FileReader(jsFile))` only on reload. |
| **Unit testing** | Use `Junit5` + `kotlin-test` to test Java logic, and `Karma` / `Mocha` to test JS modules separately. |

