Below is a **complete, self‑contained Java implementation of a very simple blockchain**.  
It contains everything you need to understand the basic mechanics: block data, hashing, proof‑of‑work, chain integrity and a tiny demo that adds a few blocks and prints the result.

> ⚠️ **This is an educational toy implementation.**  
> It does not implement networking, consensus, signatures, or a Merkle‑tree transaction set.  
> For production use, look at established libraries like Hyperledger Fabric, Tendermint, or the Java libraries that come with BitcoinJ/EthereumJ.

