## 4. Security & Production Tips

| Topic | What to do |
|-------|------------|
| **Password storage** | Always hash with `bcrypt` (or Argon2). Never store plain text. |
| **JWT secret** | Keep `JWT_SECRET` in an environment variable, never commit to repo. |
| **HTTPS** | In production, always serve via TLS. |
| **CORS** | Configure `cors()` with exact front‑end origin. |
| **Rate limiting** | Use `express-rate-limit` to avoid brute‑force. |
| **Input validation** | Use `express-validator` or `zod` to reject malformed bodies. |
| **SQL injection** | Never interpolate; always use parameterized queries (`$1`, `$2` or `?`). |
| **Environment** | Separate dev, staging, prod configs (`.env.development`, etc.). |
| **Docker** | Containerise both backend and front‑end for consistent env. |
| **Database migration** | Use `node-pg-migrate`, `sequelize-cli`, or `knex` for versioned schema. |

