  .btn { width: 23%; margin: 1%; height: 40px; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Calculator</h2>
<input type="text" id="display" readonly>
<div id="buttons">
  <div class="row"><button class="btn" data-val="7">7</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="8">8</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="9">9</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="/">÷</button></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn" data-val="4">4</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="5">5</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="6">6</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="*">×</button></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn" data-val="1">1</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="2">2</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="3">3</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="-">‑</button></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn" data-val="0">0</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val=".">.</button>
                    <button class="btn" id="clear">C</button>
                    <button class="btn" data-val="+">+</button></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn" id="equals" style="width: 98%;">=</button></div>
</div>

<script>
  const display = document.getElementById('display');
  let currentInput = '';
  let firstOperand = null;
  let operator = null;
  let awaitingSecondOperand = false;

  function updateDisplay() {
    display.value = currentInput || '0';
  }

  function handleOperator(nextOperator) {
    const inputValue = parseFloat(currentInput);

    if (operator && awaitingSecondOperand) {
      // allow operator chaining like 5 + 3 * 2
      operator = nextOperator;
      return;
    }

    if (firstOperand === null && !isNaN(inputValue)) {
      firstOperand = inputValue;
    } else if (operator) {
      const result = performCalculation(firstOperand, inputValue, operator);
      firstOperand = result;
      display.value = result;
    }

    awaitingSecondOperand = true;
    operator = nextOperator;
    currentInput = '';
  }

  function performCalculation(first, second, op) {
    switch(op) {
      case '+': return first + second;
      case '-': return first - second;
      case '*': return first * second;
      case '/': return first / second;
      default: return second;
    }
  }

  function inputDigit(digit) {
    if (awaitingSecondOperand) {
      currentInput = digit;
      awaitingSecondOperand = false;
    } else {
      currentInput = currentInput === '0' ? digit : currentInput + digit;
    }
  }

  function inputDecimal(dot) {
    if (awaitingSecondOperand) {
      currentInput = '0.';
      awaitingSecondOperand = false;
      return;
    }
    if (!currentInput.includes(dot)) {
      currentInput += dot;
    }
  }

  document.getElementById('buttons').addEventListener('click', function(e) {
    const { target } = e;
    if (!target.matches('button')) return;

    const val = target.dataset.val;

    if (target.id === 'clear') {
      currentInput = '';
      operator = null;
      firstOperand = null;
      awaitingSecondOperand = false;
      updateDisplay();
      return;
    }

    if (target.id === 'equals') {
      if (!operator || awaitingSecondOperand) return;
      const result = performCalculation(firstOperand, parseFloat(currentInput), operator);
      display.value = result;
      currentInput = result.toString();
      operator = null;
      firstOperand = null;
      awaitingSecondOperand = false;
      return;
    }

    if ('+-*/'.includes(val)) {
      handleOperator(val);
    } else if (val === '.') {
      inputDecimal(val);
    } else {
      inputDigit(val);
    }

    updateDisplay();
  });

  updateDisplay();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works
- **Display**: A read‑only text box shows the current input or result.
- **Buttons**: Number keys, operators, a decimal point, clear (`C`) and equals (`=`).
- **Logic**: Handles input, operator selection, basic chaining (`5 + 3 * 2`) and displays the final result.
- **Styling**: Very simple CSS for a clean look—feel free to tweak.

---

## 🎉  Quick Recap

| Language | Interface | How to run | Key Features |
|----------|-----------|------------|--------------|
| Python | Command‑line | `python calculator.py` | Handles +, -, *, /, ^, sqrt |
| JavaScript | Browser | Open `calculator.html` | Clickable UI, chaining, decimal support |

You now have a fully functional calculator in two popular programming languages. Happy coding!

