Below is a **complete “declarative‑plus‑code” solution** that lets you:

1. **Add a List View Action** (a lightning‑quick‑action) that opens a modal.  
2. **Upload a file** inside the modal.  
3. **Attach that file to every record that was selected in the List View**.

The solution uses only standard Salesforce features plus a tiny Apex controller and an LWC.  
No Visualforce, no heavy custom code, and it works on Lightning Experience (and Experience Builder if you want).

---

## 1.  Create the Apex Controller

```apex
/*  AttachFileToRecords.cls  */
public with sharing class AttachFileToRecords {
    @AuraEnabled
    public static void attachDocumentToRecords(List<Id> recordIds, Id contentDocumentId) {
        List<ContentDocumentLink> links = new List<ContentDocumentLink>();
        for (Id recId : recordIds) {
            links.add(new ContentDocumentLink(
                ContentDocumentId = contentDocumentId,
                LinkedEntityId    = recId,
                ShareType         = 'V',        // Viewer
                Visibility        = 'AllUsers'  // Public
            ));
        }
        insert links;
    }
}
```

> **Why this controller?**  
> * `lightning-file-upload` creates a **ContentDocument** in the background.  
> * After the upload finishes we only know the `ContentDocumentId`.  
> * We then create a **ContentDocumentLink** for each record the user selected.

---

## 2.  Create the Lightning Web Component

Create a new LWC folder `attachFileModal`:

```
src
 └─ lwc
     └─ attachFileModal
         ├─ attachFileModal.html
         ├─ attachFileModal.js
         └─ attachFileModal.js-meta.xml
```

### 2.1  attachFileModal.js

```js
import { LightningElement, api, track } from 'lwc';
import attachDocumentToRecords from '@salesforce/apex/AttachFileToRecords.attachDocumentToRecords';

export default class AttachFileModal extends LightningElement {
    // recordIds will be passed from the parent (list view action)
    @api recordIds = [];

    @track showModal = false;
    @track uploading = false;
    @track errorMsg = '';

    // The id of the uploaded file (ContentDocumentId)
    @track contentDocumentId = null;

    /* --------------------------- Public methods --------------------------- */
    /** Open the modal – called by the parent */
    openModal() {
        this.showModal = true;
        this.errorMsg = '';
        this.contentDocumentId = null;
    }

    /** Close the modal – called by the parent or after success */
    closeModal() {
        this.showModal = false;
    }

    /* --------------------------- Event handlers --------------------------- */

    // Called when user clicks the “Attach” button
    handleAttach() {
        if (!this.contentDocumentId) {
            this.errorMsg = 'Please upload a file first.';
            return;
        }

        this.uploading = true;
        attachDocumentToRecords({ recordIds: this.recordIds, contentDocumentId: this.contentDocumentId })
            .then(() => {
                this.uploading = false;
                this.closeModal();
                this.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('attachmentcompleted', { bubbles: true, composed: true }));
            })
            .catch(error => {
                this.uploading = false;
                this.errorMsg = error.body.message || 'Unexpected error';
            });
    }

    // Handles lightning-file-upload finished event
    handleUploadFinished(event) {
        const uploadedFiles = event.detail.files;
        // We only allow one file – grab the first
        if (uploadedFiles && uploadedFiles.length) {
            this.contentDocumentId = uploadedFiles[0].documentId;
            this.errorMsg = '';
        }
    }

    // Handles lightning-file-upload error
    handleUploadError(event) {
        this.errorMsg = event.detail.error || 'File upload failed';
    }
}
```

