Below is a **self‑contained HTML file** that changes the page background colour every time the user clicks anywhere on the page.  
It cycles through a predefined list of colours, but you can replace the array with any colours you like (hex, rgb, hsl, named colours, etc.).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Click‑to‑Change Background Colour</title>
<style>
    html, body {
        height: 100%;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        font-family: sans-serif;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        /* initial colour */
        background-color: #ffffff;
        transition: background-color 0.4s ease; /* nice fade */
    }
    #instruction {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        color: #333;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div id="instruction">
    Click anywhere on the page to change the background colour.<br>
    (Right‑click or middle‑click works too!)
</div>

<script>
    // Array of colours you want to cycle through
    const colours = [
        '#ff5959', // red
        '#ffb400', // orange
        '#00d4ff', // light blue
        '#7b5e83', // purple
        '#4CAF50', // green
        '#FF69B4', // hot pink
        '#87CEEB', // sky blue
        '#F0E68C', // khaki
        '#E6E6FA', // lavender
        '#FFF5EE'  // seashell
    ];

    let index = 0; // keep track of the current colour

    // Helper to set background
    function setBackground(colour) {
        document.body.style.backgroundColor = colour;
    }

    // Cycle to the next colour
    function nextColour() {
        index = (index + 1) % colours.length; // wrap around
        setBackground(colours[index]);
    }

    // Initialise with the first colour (optional)
    setBackground(colours[index]);

    // Add click listener to the whole document
    document.addEventListener('click', nextColour);

    // OPTIONAL: also change colour on middle‑click (button 2)
    document.addEventListener('auxclick', function(e) {
        if (e.button === 1) nextColour();
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Colours array** – List of hex colour codes.  
   Replace or extend this array to change which colours appear.

2. **`index`** – Keeps track of which colour is currently displayed.

3. **`setBackground(colour)`** – Simple helper to set the `background-color` style on the `<body>`.

4. **`nextColour()`** – Advances the `index` (wrapping around) and updates the background.

5. **Event listeners**  
   * `click` – Fired for left‑mouse clicks (and taps on touchscreens).  
   * `auxclick` – Optional; triggers on middle‑click (mouse wheel click).  
   Both call `nextColour()`.

6. **CSS `transition`** – Gives a smooth fade between colours.

Feel free to modify the colours, add more UI, or adapt the logic to suit your project. Happy coding!

