## 6.  Going further

| Idea | How to implement |
|------|------------------|
| **Keep‑alive** | Send `ping` every 30 s; close socket on timeout. |
| **Room / channel** | Add a `room` field to the JSON message; maintain a map of rooms. |
| **Persist history** | Store messages in a lightweight DB (SQLite or Redis). |
| **User authentication** | Add a login step, store JWTs, verify in WebSocket handshake. |
| **Rate limiting** | Drop messages if a client sends > 10 msg/s. |
| **Client side** | Use a framework (React/Vue) to build a full‑featured UI. |

