Below is a **single‑file** example that shows how you can build a very small calculator with **HTML**, **CSS**, and **PHP**.  
The calculator will:

1. Ask for two numbers.  
2. Let you choose an operation (`+ – * /`).  
3. Send the data to PHP (server side).  
4. Return the result back to the same page.

> **Why PHP?**  
> PHP runs on the server, so the calculation is performed once the user submits the form.  
> It also protects you from having to write JavaScript and lets you keep the logic in one place.

